Package: clr
Title: Context Likelihood of Relatedness as Iterative Attention
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Boris", family = "Hayete",
    email = "rimorob@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    comment = "Email is a placeholder GitHub noreply address")
Description: Reframes the Context Likelihood of Relatedness (CLR) network
    inference algorithm as an early form of attention over continuous data
    distributions. Provides a B-spline mutual-information estimator (ported
    from the original CLR C sources), CLR calibration (Euclidean and the new
    Stouffer bilateral combination, plus Rayleigh and KDE variants), sparse
    row-stochastic attention operators, and iterative diffusion, orchestrated
    by the R6 class ClrAttention.
